---
import Prose from '../layouts/Prose.astro';
import { company } from '../content/company';
---

<Prose
  title="Privacy policy"
  eyebrow="Your data"
  description="How Lorapay collects, uses and protects personal data on this website and its waitlist, under the Nigeria Data Protection Act 2023."
  updated={company.policyDate}
>
  <p class="lead">
    This policy explains what personal data {company.legalName} ("Lorapay", "we") collects through this website and its waitlist,
    why, and the rights you have under the Nigeria Data Protection Act 2023 (NDPA). The Lorapay app has its own
    <a href="/app-privacy">app privacy policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
  <p>
    {company.legalName} (RC {company.rcNumber}), {company.address}, is the data controller. For anything about your data, contact
    our Data Protection Officer at <a href={`mailto:${company.privacyEmail}`}>{company.privacyEmail}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>What we collect</h2>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>When</th><th>What</th><th>Why</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td>You join the waitlist</td>
        <td>Name, mobile number, email (if you give it), state, what you'd use Lorapay for, and how you found us (for example a link you followed)</td>
        <td>To tell you when Lorapay opens in your state, and to understand where people want it</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>You send a message</td>
        <td>Name, email, topic and your message</td>
        <td>To reply to you</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>You visit the site</td>
        <td>Standard server logs kept by our hosting provider (IP address, browser, pages requested, time)</td>
        <td>To keep the site running and secure</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>This website does not use advertising or analytics cookies, and doesn't track you across other sites.</p>
  <p>Please don't send us your PIN, BVN, card or bank details. We never ask for them through this website.</p>

  <h2>Our lawful basis</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Consent</strong> for the waitlist: you tick the box when you join. You can withdraw it at any time.</li>
    <li><strong>Legitimate interests</strong> for replying to messages you send us and keeping the site secure.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Waitlist details: until we've told you Lorapay is open in your state and 12 months after that, or until you ask us to remove you, whichever comes first.</li>
    <li>Messages: up to 24 months after our last reply.</li>
    <li>Server logs: as kept by our hosting provider, for no more than 30 days.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
  <p>We don't sell your data or share it for marketing. We use service providers who process it for us under contract:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Google</strong> (Google Workspace / Google Sheets) to store waitlist entries and messages.</li>
    <li><strong>Vercel</strong> to host this website.</li>
    <li><strong>Termii</strong> to send the launch message by SMS, when we send it.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Google and Vercel store data outside Nigeria, including in the United States. We protect these transfers with the safeguards
    that sections 41 to 43 of the NDPA require, including contracts that bind these providers to protect the data. We may also
    disclose data where the law requires it.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>Under the NDPA you can ask us to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>tell you what data we hold about you and give you a copy;</li>
    <li>correct it if it's wrong;</li>
    <li>delete it, or remove you from the waitlist;</li>
    <li>restrict or object to how we use it;</li>
    <li>send it to you or another organisation in a common format;</li>
    <li>withdraw your consent, at any time, without affecting what we did before.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Email <a href={`mailto:${company.privacyEmail}`}>{company.privacyEmail}</a> from the address or phone number you used. We'll
    answer within 30 days. If you're not happy with our answer, you can complain to the Nigeria Data Protection Commission (NDPC).
  </p>

  <h2>Security</h2>
  <p>
    Waitlist entries are sent over an encrypted connection (HTTPS) and stored in an account protected by two-step verification,
    which only the Lorapay staff who need it can open.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>Lorapay is for people aged 18 and over. Please don't join the waitlist if you're younger.</p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>If we change this policy we'll update the date at the top, and tell waitlist members about important changes.</p>
</Prose>
